    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.johnson - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.johnson.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.johnson()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find all-pairs shortest paths with Johnson's algorithm (negative weights\n    allowed).\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.johnson()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: >-\n    Find all-pairs shortest paths with Johnson's algorithm (negative weights\n    allowed).\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.johnson()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Find all-pairs shortest paths with Johnson's algorithm (negative weights\n  allowed).\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nFind all-pairs shortest paths with Johnson's algorithm (negative weights allowed).\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L62742-L62848){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.johnson(weighted=None)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Johnson all-pairs shortest paths](../assets/graphs/johnson.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three nodes with directed weighted edges A to B 4, A to C 2 and C to B −1. Johnson's algorithm reweights the edges to remove the negative one without changing which paths are shortest, then runs Dijkstra from every node. The path it returns from A to B is A, C, B (accent color), costing 2 + (−1) = 1, less than the direct edge's 4.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nJohnson's algorithm computes a shortest path between every pair of nodes on a graph that\nmay have negative edge weights (but no negative cycles). It reweights the edges with\nnode potentials so that all weights become non-negative without changing which paths are\nshortest, then runs Dijkstra's algorithm from every node. On sparse graphs it is much\nfaster than `floyd_warshall()`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to use edge weights. If `None` (default), follows the graph's `weighted`\n    flag.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [dict[int, dict[int, list[int]]]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   `result[source][target]` is a shortest path as node IDs, for every reachable pair.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph has a negative cycle (or an undirected graph has a negative edge).\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nBellman-Ford from a virtual source joined to every node gives potentials $h$ with\n$w'(u, v) = w(u, v) + h(u) - h(v) \\ge 0$; every path's reweighted length differs from its\ntrue length by $h(s) - h(t)$, so shortest paths are preserved (Johnson, 1977). Total time\n$O(VE + V E \\log V)$. Path lengths match NetworkX's `johnson`.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~floyd_warshall`) \n\n:   All-pairs distances, from a dense algorithm.\n\n[](`~goldberg_radzik`) \n\n:   Shortest paths from one source, with negative weights.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe direct edge from A to B costs `4`, but the route through C costs `2 + (-1) = 1`:\n\n::: {#5c7745aa .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"A\", \"B\", 4.0), (\"A\", \"C\", 2.0), (\"C\", \"B\", -1.0)], directed=True\n)\n\npaths = graph.johnson()\na, b = graph.get_id_from_label(\"A\"), graph.get_id_from_label(\"B\")\n[graph.get_label_from_id(n) for n in paths[a][b]]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n['A', 'C', 'B']\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Which quotes are worth using\n\n`currency()` holds the exchange rates quoted between six currencies, each edge weighted by\nthe negative log of its rate, so that the path of least weight is the conversion that\nyields the most. With `arbitrage=False`, no cycle has a negative total weight. Johnson's\nalgorithm finds the best route between every pair of currencies, and 14 of the 30 go\nthrough another currency:\n\n::: {#a70fe920 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nfx = ec.currency(arbitrage=False)\npaths = fx.johnson()\nlabel = fx.get_label_from_id\n\nindirect = [\n    [label(n) for n in path]\n    for targets in paths.values()\n    for path in targets.values()\n    if len(path) > 2\n]\nlen(indirect), indirect[:4]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(14,\n [['EUR', 'USD', 'CAD'],\n  ['GBP', 'USD', 'JPY'],\n  ['GBP', 'USD', 'CHF'],\n  ['GBP', 'USD', 'CAD']])\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nEvery indirect route goes through the US dollar. Of the 18 quotes, only the two between\nthe yen and the Swiss franc (highlighted) are never part of a best route, since going\nthrough the dollar always yields more:\n\n::: {#4930a616 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nused = {\n    (u, v)\n    for targets in paths.values()\n    for path in targets.values()\n    for u, v in zip(path, path[1:])\n}\nedges = fx.get_edge_df()\nunused = [\n    (u, v) for u, v in zip(edges[\"source\"], edges[\"target\"])\n    if (u, v) not in used\n]\nfx.plot(highlight=unused, label_by=\"label\", curved_edges=True, seed=4)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-6